<title>USA: GM unit files for $500 mln shelf debt offer.</title>
<headline>GM unit files for $500 mln shelf debt offer.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>General Motors Acceptance Corp, a General Motors Corp unit, filed Friday a shelf registration with the Securities and Exchange Commission for up to $500 million in debt offering known as SmartNotes.</p>
<p>The notes are due from nine months from date of issue and net proceeds will be used to purchase receivables, make loans and repay debt, the company said.</p>
<p>The offering will be made through Chicago Corp, A.G. Edwards &amp; Sons Inc, Edward D Jones &amp; Co L.P., Prudential Securities Inc and Smith Barney Inc.</p>
</text>
